{
  "_comment": [
    "A faithful mirror of expected.json, as a read of a correctly-built file would produce it. The diff",
    "of the two MUST be empty, and every arm must be able to RUN against it — that baseline is what makes",
    "actual-dirty.json's 'reports exactly these' a real claim rather than one satisfiable by a diff that",
    "reports everything.",
    "",
    "It is not a byte copy, and every difference is deliberate — each one is a representation the reader",
    "really produces and the diff has to reconcile, so the baseline exercises all three reconciliations",
    "rather than leaving them unproven. A byte copy would pass while every lenience was dead.",
    "",
    "  1. expected.json claims `/glyph descendantFills`; this carries the ink one level down on",
    "     `/glyph/Vector fills`, which is where a reader finds it beneath a plain container.",
    "  2. expected.json claims one uniform `/ strokeWeight`; this carries the four per-side weights Figma",
    "     actually stores, all agreeing. `boundVariables` never contains `strokeWeight` in a real read.",
    "  3. `/label` carries the three font fields ALONGSIDE its text style, as a node with a style applied",
    "     does — so the clean run also proves those three are not reported as unplanned extras.",
    "  4. `/focusRing` is an INSTANCE carrying a binding the engine plans nowhere here, because an instance",
    "     surfaces its main component's bindings as its own. The clean run must stay clean and say so in a",
    "     note — reported, it would be one of 2,705 in a real read.",
    "  5. No text style carries `fontWeight`. Figma has no such property — it has `fontName.style` — so a",
    "     read cannot produce one, and the engine's planned weight is checked THROUGH `fontStyle`. Here all",
    "     three styles bind `fontStyle` to a variable, so the weight rides on that binding and the clean run",
    "     must not report three missing properties.",
    "  6. The `shared` collection, `fix/shared/brand/500` and the `body/lg/default` text style are all",
    "     planned by the engine and all ABSENT from the local tables, because this file consumes them from a",
    "     published library — see `libraryConsumed`. Absent and library-sourced is not absent: the clean run",
    "     must stay clean and put a count in a note. Delete `libraryConsumed` and three false findings appear,",
    "     which is exactly what the harness did before Gap B was closed."
  ],
